{"name":"Flock of Seagulls","hex":"#b6bfbd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flock","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A number of birds together in a group, such as those gathered together for the purpose of migration.\nA large number of animals associated together in a group; commonly used of sheep, but  also used for goats or other livestock animals, or sometimes any group of animals.\n\nThe group of sheep being watched by one shepherd.\nA large number of people.","A large number of animals associated together in a group; commonly used of sheep, but  also used for goats or other livestock animals, or sometimes any group of animals."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To congregate in or head towards a place in large numbers.","To flock to; to crowd."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flock"},{"term":"seagulls","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of seagull"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seagulls"}],"entries":[{"title":"A Flock of Seagulls","blocks":[{"text":"A Flock of Seagulls are an English new wave band formed in Liverpool in 1979. The group, whose best-known line-up comprised Mike Score, Ali Score, Frank Maudsley and Paul Reynolds, hit the peak of their chart success in the early 1980s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Mike_Score.jpg/330px-Mike_Score.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Flock_of_Seagulls"},{"title":"Gull","blocks":[{"text":"Gulls, informally called seagulls, are seabirds of the subfamily Larinae. They are most closely related to terns and skimmers, and are placed with them in the family Laridae. They are also related, more distantly, to auks and skuas, and more distantly still to waders. Until the 21st century, most gulls were placed in the genus Larus, but that arrangement is now considered polyphyletic, leading to the readoption and revision of several genera."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Herring_Gull_%28Larus_argentatus%29%2C_Brighton%2C_England.JPG/330px-Herring_Gull_%28Larus_argentatus%29%2C_Brighton%2C_England.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gull"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/A_Flock_of_Seagulls_in_2012.jpg/500px-A_Flock_of_Seagulls_in_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/A_Flock_of_Seagulls_in_2012.jpg/1280px-A_Flock_of_Seagulls_in_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/A_Flock_of_Seagulls_in_2012.jpg/500px-A_Flock_of_Seagulls_in_2012.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Flock Of Seagulls live, 2012.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Flock_of_Seagulls_in_2012.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/A_Flock_of_Seagulls_in_2024.jpg/500px-A_Flock_of_Seagulls_in_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/A_Flock_of_Seagulls_in_2024.jpg/500px-A_Flock_of_Seagulls_in_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Flock of Seagulls performing at Harbison Theatre in Irmo, South Carolina in 2024","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Flock_of_Seagulls_in_2024.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg/500px-Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_fli